0 Ring persistent, membranous, sheathed below, with granulose underside and filamentous upper surface, cap finely granulose. Cystidia absent; sp amyloid011113602
0 Ring evanescent, with granulose veil extending down the stem011213705
0 Cap and stem pale lilaceous or pink to almost white; smell and taste unpleasant. Sp 4-5.5 x 3-5 µm (Fig. 127); KOH hardly discolouring cuticular cells of cap. - Mossy forests, needle beds, heaps of debris; especially late autumn. D&D 321, MLge, R&H 420. 02131490 C. carcharias (Pers.) Konr. & Maubl.0
0 Cap and stem rusty ochraceous; smell and taste not distinctive. KOH discolouring the cuticular cells dark rusty brown0214141003
0 Cap rusty brown (rarely medium brown or ochre), distinctly granulose. Sp 4-5 x 3-3.5 µm , mostly broadly ellipsoid to subglobose (Fig. 128). – Mossy forests. SZP 35: 117, M&J III Calocybe 4. 034515120 C. fallax Smith & Sing.0
0 Cap ochre or fulvous brown , finely granulose. Sp longer than above0346151304
0 Frb fairly slender; cap ochre; stem with fairly narrow ring. Sp 5-6 x 2.5-3.5 µm, ellipsoid. 046716150 C. intermedium Harmaja0
0 Frb stouter; cap slightly brighter, fulvous brown; ring fairly broad. Sp 5-7 x 3.5-4.5 µm, mostly broadly ellipsoid to subglobose. 046816160 C. tuomikoskii Harmaja0
0 Sp amyloid. Cap yellowish or brownish ochre to dark brown0529171806
