0 Stem apex, above the annular zone, pale purple to dark violet when fresh, intensely violet when dry; frb small, cap pale to dark brown without yellowish tinge, surface very finely granulose; flesh pale without yellow tinge. Sp ± fusoid, 6-7.5 x 3.5-5 µm. - Among mosses (esp . Polytrichum), esp. on rock outcrops, also in bogs; late in the season . BSMF 89 pl 1. 0691118210 C. lilacipes Harmaja 120
0///(= C longisporum (Kuhn.) Heinem. & Thoen var. purpurascens Heinem. & Thoen nom. inval.).///C. saarenoksae Harmaja differs esp. in yellow brown colours.///C. niveum Harmaja differs esp. in being white0691218220N0
0 Stem apex yellowish to brownish, rarely with a faint purplish tinge at least when dry06913182307
0 Flesh of cap distinctly yellow in upper part, otherwise ochre; cap yellowish brown or paler; gills yellow. Sp 6-7.5 x 3-5 µm, ± fusoid (Fig. 130); arthrospores abundant in upper part of cap flesh. - Mossy forests. D&S 320, lower right fig., Cke 1113/ 935, R&H 421. 07131419250 C. jasonis (Cooke & Massee) Harmaja 150
0///(= C. amianthinum var. longisporum Kühn.)07131519260N0
0 Flesh white throughout; cap brown to yellowish, granules often small; gills whitish. Sp 5-7 x 2.5-3 µm, ellipsoid to oblong (Fig. 126); arthrospores lacking or rare. - Among mosses in forests and heaths. D&D 320 (upper row), Phil 31, R&H 420. 07131619270 C. amianthinum (Scop.) Konr. & Maubl.0
0 Frb snow white, at least when young; cap with pointed scales which soon fall away. Sp 4-5.5 x 2.5-3 /µm (Fig. 125). - Forests and bogs, among mosses. Bres 50. 08101720290 C. ambrosii (Bres.) Sing.0
0 Frb coloured081018203009
0 Cap dark rusty to vinaceous brown, fading to pale sordid brownish. Sp 3.5-5 x 2.5-3 µm (Fig. 129). - Forests and heaths, roadsides, rarely in bogs. MLge, Mossb II 65 , R&H 421. 09181921320 C. granulosum (Batsch:Fr.) Kuhn.0
0 Cap some shade of red or orange0918202133010
0 Cap brownish cinnabar to reddish orange; stem often stout, with subbulbose base and usually with copious patches of the red velar coating at least at and below annular zone. Sp 3.5-5 x 2-3(-3.5) µm (Fig. 131); cystidia slightly vcntricose below, tapering to a long, narrow neck with spear-shaped apex often covered with crystals. - Forests, among mosses or on needle beds. FAD 15 F, R&H 422 , C 411. 010202122350 C. terrei (Berk. & Br.) Harmaja 220
0///(= C cinnabarinum (Alb. & Schw.) Konr. & Maubl.)010202222360N0
0 Cap bright reddish orange to orange yellow; stem usually more slender, below annular zone mainly coated by the pure white filamentous inner velar layer, coloured velar remnants small and scarce, mostly situated near the base; gills more broadly adnate, even subdecurrent. Sp 3.5-4.5 x 2.5-3 µm ; cystidia absent. - Mossy ground in forests. Miller 110 (sub C. amianthinum). 010202322370 C. adnatifolium (Peck) Harmaja 240
